# The sleep wallpapers (docs in sleep/README.md) are the user's own pictures:
# they are put in a folder on the store, which preinit mounts read-write at
# /kindle-us while the policy is not loaded yet (preinit/PreInit.c,
# testfile_handover_store), so the folder and its files carry the vfat label.
# The display HAL reads them when the screen goes off
# (gralloc/framebuffer.cpp, wallpaperSleepLocked); nothing else SurfaceFlinger
# does touches the store, so this is read-only and no wider than it has to be.
#
# The rule is needed, and not redundant with the base policy: the sepolicy this
# port ships has nothing from surfaceflinger to vfat -- `sesearch -A -s
# surfaceflinger -t vfat` over the image's own precompiled policy finds only
# "allow domain fs_type:dir getattr". Without the rule the HAL gets EACCES,
# falls back to the picture that ships in the image, and the feature is off.
#
# Coordination: this file is under device/amazon/pw3/sepolicy, which T13's AOSP
# build compiles into the ramdisk's precompiled policy. It is a two-line
# addition next to gralloc.pw3.so; whoever merges the wallpaper branch should
# carry it in the same PR as the HAL change (see readom-port/reports/
# t10-sleepwall-impl.md, "SELinux").
allow surfaceflinger vfat:dir r_dir_perms;
allow surfaceflinger vfat:file r_file_perms;
